; Both kernels have the same loop, which is a run of eight VMEM stores. The
; placement would add s_nop before the loop of @vmem_nopreload. @vmem_preload
; has inreg arguments, so they are preloaded into SGPRs. The preload prologue
; is inserted after this pass, and it moves the kernel body to a 256 byte
; aligned offset. The pass does not know the final offsets, so it skips the
; kernel. The loop of @vmem_preload has no s_nop, and only @vmem_nopreload is
; reported in the debug output.

; PRINT: fetch-window: vmem_nopreload
; PRINT-NOT: fetch-window: vmem_preload

